1
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:24,000
One steals. One kills. One dies.

2
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:42,000
The Missouri Breaks is a western, drama film directed by Arthur Penn.

3
00:18:54,000 --> 00:19:00,000
When vigilante land baron David Braxton hangs one of the best friends of cattle rustler Tom Logan,
Logan's gang decides to get even by purchasing a small farm next to Braxton's ranch.

4
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:18,000
From there the rustlers begin stealing horses, using
the farm as a front for their operation.

5
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Determined to stop the thefts at any cost, Braxton retains the
services of eccentric sharpshooter Robert E.

6
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:54,000
Lee Clayton, who begins ruthlessly taking down Logan's gang.

7
00:44:06,000 --> 00:44:12,000
Robert E. Lee Clayton, played by Marlon Brando.

8
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:30,000
Tom Logan, played by Jack Nicholson.

9
00:56:42,000 --> 00:56:48,000
Tittle Tod, played by Randy Quaid.

10
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Jane Braxton, played by Kathleen Lloyd.

11
01:09:18,000 --> 01:09:24,000
Cary, played by Frederic Forrest.

12
01:15:36,000 --> 01:15:42,000
Calvin, played by Harry Dean Stanton.

13
01:21:54,000 --> 01:22:00,000
The Missouri Breaks is a 1976 American Western film
starring Marlon Brando and Jack Nicholson.

14
01:28:12,000 --> 01:28:18,000
The film was directed by Arthur Penn, with supporting performances by Randy Quaid, Harry Dean
Stanton, Frederic Forrest, John McLiam, and Kathleen Lloyd in her film debut.

15
01:34:30,000 --> 01:34:36,000
The score was composed by John Williams.

16
01:40:48,000 --> 01:40:54,000
The title of the film refers to a forlorn and very rugged area of  north-central Montana, where
over eons, the Missouri River has made countless deep cuts or "breaks" in the land.

17
01:47:06,000 --> 01:47:12,000
The film explores themes including the American frontier
myth, economic exploitation and law and order.

18
01:53:24,000 --> 01:53:30,000
Like some other films directed by Penn, it has been read as an
allegory of capitalism and the American counterculture.

19
01:59:42,000 --> 01:59:48,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
